TORUS KNOT T(p, q) — EQUATIONS, NOTATION, AND FUNDAMENTALS

PARAMETRIC REPRESENTATION (R = 1)
  r(t) = 1 + rho * cos(q * t)
  x(t) = r(t) * cos(p * t)
  y(t) = r(t) * sin(p * t)
  z(t) = rho * sin(q * t)
  0 <= t <= 2*pi

ASSOCIATED TORUS
  (sqrt(x^2 + y^2) - 1)^2 + z^2 = rho^2

PARAMETERS
  t   : parameter
  p   : longitudinal windings (around the axis)
  q   : meridional windings (through the hole)
  rho : minor radius
  T(p,q) : torus knot or link

KNOT vs LINK
  d = gcd(p, q)
  d = 1 => single knot
  d > 1 => link with d components

SYMMETRY
  T(p, q) equivalent to T(q, p)
  T(-p, q) and T(p, -q) are mirror images

TRIVIAL CASES
  |p| = 1 or |q| = 1 => unknot

CROSSING NUMBER (coprime positive p, q)
  c = min( p*(q - 1), q*(p - 1) )
  If p < q then c = q*(p - 1)
  If q < p then c = p*(q - 1)

GENUS = UNKNOTTING NUMBER
  g = u = (p - 1)*(q - 1) / 2

ALEXANDER POLYNOMIAL
  Delta(t) = (t^(p*q) - 1)*(t - 1)
             / ((t^p - 1)*(t^q - 1))

THE NINE KNOTS FROM THE 3x3 GRID
(All have gcd(p, q) = 1)

